#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 8637..9195
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/8
msgid ""
"Guess I should probably pull the plug on those, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来那些也得由我亲手关掉了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 9209..10253
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/9
msgid ""
"Good idea. What else... Well,\n"
msgstr ""
"好主意。还有呢……嗯，\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 10253..12009
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/10
msgid ""
"as with all AI machines, you can incapacitate the\n"
"entire unit by taking out the AI itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"和所有AI兵器一样，只要\n"
"破坏AI本体，整台就会瘫痪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 12023..13235
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/11
msgid ""
"If you can get the hatch open and climb inside, you\n"
"can pull out the memory boards -\n"
msgstr ""
"只要打开舱盖爬进去，\n"
"把记忆板拔出来——\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13249..13722
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/12
msgid ""
"lights out, AI.\n"
msgstr ""
"AI就断气了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 13736..14544
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/13
msgid ""
"We may be able to use those boards for ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"那些板子我们也许能自己用上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 14558..15701
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/14
msgid ""
"If you can, try and get inside the AI pod and have\n"
"a crack at it.\n"
msgstr ""
"可以的话，想办法钻进AI舱\n"
"试试看。\n"

#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 15729..17066
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/15
msgid ""
"You won't be able to do that until you've damaged\n"
"it enough to stop it from moving, first.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过得先把它打伤到动不了，\n"
"否则你靠不近。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 17080..17860
#: codec/1/255/0xffda0/16
msgid ""
"Got it. Usual tactics first, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白了。那就先按老办法来。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/0
msgid ""
"Being an unmanned vehicle,\n"
msgstr ""
"作为无人载具，\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/1
msgid ""
"the Chrysalis can perform extreme G-force\n"
"maneuvers that standard aircraft can't.\n"
msgstr ""
"Chrysalis能够执行普通飞机无法做到的\n"
"极限G力机动。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/2
msgid ""
"It'll be difficult to counter-attack once it's coming\n"
"at you.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦它朝你冲过来，就很难\n"
"反击了。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/3
msgid ""
"I should mention that it's also equipped with a\n"
"railgun.\n"
msgstr ""
"我应该提一下，它还配备了一门\n"
"轨道炮。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/4
msgid ""
"A what?\n"
msgstr ""
"装有什么？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/5
msgid ""
"A weapon that fires rounds using electromagnetic\n"
"force in lieu of gunpowder.\n"
msgstr ""
"一种用电磁力而非火药\n"
"发射弹丸的武器。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/6
msgid ""
"Wait... An electric weapon?\n"
msgstr ""
"等等……电击武器？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/7
msgid ""
"Not exactly. The rounds themselves are\n"
"conventional shells.\n"
msgstr ""
"不完全是。弹丸本身是\n"
"常规炮弹。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/8
msgid ""
"It creates force by running an electric current\n"
"through a magnetic field.\n"
msgstr ""
"它通过让电流穿过磁场\n"
"来产生力。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/9
msgid ""
"Fleming's left-hand rule - didn't they teach you that\n"
"at school?\n"
msgstr ""
"弗莱明左手定则——学校没教过你\n"
"这个吗？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/10
msgid ""
"Not at mine.\n"
msgstr ""
"我学校没教。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/11
msgid ""
"Oh. Anyway, as the railgun uses electromagnetic\n"
"force,\n"
msgstr ""
"哦。总之，由于轨道炮使用电磁\n"
"力，\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/12
msgid ""
"it needs to charge before firing.\n"
msgstr ""
"开火前需要充能。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/13
msgid ""
"Once you see it starting to charge, take immediate\n"
"evasive action.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦发现它开始充能，立即采取\n"
"回避行动。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/14
msgid ""
"Also, as with the Pupa, destroying the AI will put\n"
"the unit out of commission.\n"
msgstr ""
"另外，和蛹一样，摧毁AI会让\n"
"该单位瘫痪。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/15
msgid ""
"Do enough damage and it'll have to land.\n"
msgstr ""
"伤害够了它就得降落。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/16
msgid ""
"Use that opportunity to get in the AI pod.\n"
msgstr ""
"趁此机会进入AI舱。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/17
msgid ""
"Wait too long, and it'll start to repair itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"拖太久它会开始自我修复。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/18
msgid ""
"Be sure to shoot the hatch the moment it lands.\n"
msgstr ""
"降落的瞬间务必射击舱门。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x1003f0/19
msgid ""
"I think I can handle that.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个我能应付。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/0
msgid ""
"During development, I had trouble figuring out how\n"
"to handle the Cocoon's excess heat.\n"
msgstr ""
"在开发过程中，我很难弄清楚如何\n"
"处理茧的多余热量。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/1
msgid ""
"I'm embarrassed to admit it, but the radiators are\n"
"most likely its weakest points.\n"
msgstr ""
"我很不好意思承认，但散热器\n"
"很可能是它最薄弱的部位。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/2
msgid ""
"They're not heavily armored, as heat wasn't\n"
"dissipating properly.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们没有厚重的装甲，因为热量无法\n"
"正常散发。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/3
msgid ""
"Where are they?\n"
msgstr ""
"在哪里？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/4
msgid ""
"There are multiple radiators on the upper and\n"
"lower sections.\n"
msgstr ""
"在上部和\n"
"下部有多个散热器。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/5
msgid ""
"Just look for the exhaust fumes.\n"
msgstr ""
"找排气烟雾就行。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/6
msgid ""
"Only thing is, the upper radiators typically aren't\n"
"exposed.\n"
msgstr ""
"问题是，上部散热器通常不会\n"
"暴露。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/7
msgid ""
"You should probably shoot for the lower ones first.\n"
msgstr ""
"最好先打下面的。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/8
msgid ""
"You could move under its body to access the\n"
"lower ones,\n"
msgstr ""
"你可移到它身下接触\n"
"下部散热器，\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/9
msgid ""
"but the Cocoon is capable of vertical movement,\n"
"so be careful not to get crushed.\n"
msgstr ""
"但茧能够垂直移动，\n"
"所以小心不要被压扁。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/10
msgid ""
"Watch out for missiles and hedgehogs too.\n"
msgstr ""
"也要提防导弹和刺猬弹。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/11
msgid ""
"Hedgehogs? Anti-submarine multiple spigot\n"
"mortars?\n"
msgstr ""
"刺猬弹？反潜多管\n"
"迫击炮？\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/12
msgid ""
"I adapted the technology for use as a surface\n"
"weapon.\n"
msgstr ""
"我改造技术，用作水面\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/13
msgid ""
"Both the missiles and hedgehogs take time to load,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过，导弹和刺猬都需要时间\n"
"装填。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/14
msgid ""
"It can't fire a hedgehog until the lamp comes on.\n"
msgstr ""
"指示灯亮起前它无法发射刺猬弹。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/15
msgid ""
"As for the missiles, watch for the way the hatches\n"
"move.\n"
msgstr ""
"至于导弹，注意舱门\n"
"移动的方式。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/16
msgid ""
"That'll be my chance to get close.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就是我靠近的机会。\n"

#: codec/1/256/0x100aa0/17
msgid ""
"When the hatches open, out come the missiles.\n"
msgstr ""
"舱门一开，导弹就出来了。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/0
msgid ""
"...Number of warheads detected by the DEW Line?\n"
msgstr ""
"……预警线探测到的弹头数量？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/1
msgid ""
"Fifty-seven.\n"
msgstr ""
"五十七枚。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/2
msgid ""
"Number of MIRVs included?\n"
msgstr ""
"分导多弹头多少？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/3
msgid ""
"Minimum twenty-nine, maximum thirty-five.\n"
msgstr ""
"最少二十九，最多三十五。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/4
msgid ""
"Target region?\n"
msgstr ""
"目标区？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/5
msgid ""
"United States. East Coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国。东海岸。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/6
msgid ""
"Estimated time of reentry?\n"
msgstr ""
"预计再入时间？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/7
msgid ""
"Two-oh-four-eight Zulu.\n"
msgstr ""
"祖鲁时间二〇四八。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/8
msgid ""
"President's selected attack option?\n"
msgstr ""
"总统选定的攻击方案？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/9
msgid ""
"Unknown.\n"
msgstr ""
"不明。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/10
msgid ""
"The President is dead?\n"
msgstr ""
"总统死了？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/11
msgid ""
"Unknown. Communication has been lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"不明。通讯已中断。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/12
msgid ""
"...I select Offutt Air Force Base as my target.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我选奥福特空军基地为目标。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/13
msgid ""
"Offutt...? But that's a U.S. base! What on earth do\n"
"you mean?!\n"
msgstr ""
"奥福特……？那是美国基地！你什么\n"
"意思？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/14
msgid ""
"Based on the projected number of incoming\n"
"warheads,\n"
msgstr ""
"根据预测的来袭\n"
"弹头数量，\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/15
msgid ""
"Washington D.C. is presumed destroyed.\n"
msgstr ""
"华盛顿特区推定已被摧毁。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/16
msgid ""
"The President is most likely dead, the U.S.\n"
"government's control lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"总统很可能已经死亡，美国\n"
"政府已失去控制。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/17
msgid ""
"I realize that. So why not retaliate?!\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。那为何不报复？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/18
msgid ""
"With both sides destroyed, global anarchy would\n"
"ensue.\n"
msgstr ""
"双方被毁后，全球将陷入\n"
"无政府状态。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/19
msgid ""
"Recovery would be... difficult.\n"
msgstr ""
"恢复将……极为困难。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/20
msgid ""
"The United States' nuclear strike capability must\n"
"therefore be neutralized\n"
msgstr ""
"因此，美国的核打击能力必须\n"
"被消除，\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/21
msgid ""
"in order to preserve the Communist bloc, where\n"
"government remains largely intact.\n"
msgstr ""
"以保全共产主义阵营，那里\n"
"政府大体上仍然完好。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/22
msgid ""
"You're siding with the enemy? You can't be serious!\n"
msgstr ""
"你站在敌人那边？你不是认真的吧！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/23
msgid ""
"...Tell me, how do you define enemy?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你如何定义敌人？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/24
msgid ""
"There are no borders in this world.\n"
msgstr ""
"这世上没有国界。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/25
msgid ""
"The same conclusion, again and again... Where is\n"
"the flaw?\n"
msgstr ""
"同样结论，一次又一次……破绽\n"
"在哪？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/26
msgid ""
"All right. Let's try something else. Commencing test.\n"
msgstr ""
"好吧。换个方式。开始测试。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/27
msgid ""
"Understood.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/28
msgid ""
"...You're crossing a suspension bridge.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你正走过一座吊桥。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/29
msgid ""
"Is this my mission?\n"
msgstr ""
"这是我任务？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/30
msgid ""
"Yes. Your destination is the other side.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。你的目的地是对岸。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/31
msgid ""
"The bridge is wide enough for only one person to\n"
"pass at a time.\n"
msgstr ""
"这座桥很窄，一次只能让一个人\n"
"通过。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/32
msgid ""
"A man is approaching from the opposite side. He's\n"
"carrying a gun.\n"
msgstr ""
"对面有个人正在靠近。他\n"
"手里拿着一把枪。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/33
msgid ""
"I shoot him.\n"
msgstr ""
"我开枪打他。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/34
msgid ""
"Suppose he's your husband?\n"
msgstr ""
"假如他是你丈夫？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/35
msgid ""
"...I shoot him.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我开枪打他。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/36
msgid ""
"In self defense?\n"
msgstr ""
"自卫？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/37
msgid ""
"To spare him the grief. One must die, and one\n"
"must live.\n"
msgstr ""
"免他悲伤。必须死一个，活\n"
"一个。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/38
msgid ""
"...Next question.\n"
msgstr ""
"……下一个问题。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/39
msgid ""
"Your father asks you to fix the roof and mow the\n"
"lawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"你父亲让你去修屋顶，还要修剪\n"
"草坪。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/40
msgid ""
"When you climb the ladder onto the roof, the\n"
"ladder is taken away.\n"
msgstr ""
"当你爬上梯子到屋顶时，梯子\n"
"被拿走了。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/41
msgid ""
"I fix the roof.\n"
msgstr ""
"我修屋顶。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/42
msgid ""
"And when you're finished?\n"
msgstr ""
"修完之后呢？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/43
msgid ""
"I jump down.\n"
msgstr ""
"我跳下去。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/44
msgid ""
"You'll break more than bones at this height.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个高度，断的不只是骨头。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/45
msgid ""
"I see no need to change my decision. I have not\n"
"finished mowing the lawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"我看没必要改变我的决定。我还没\n"
"修剪完草坪。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/46
msgid ""
"I must remain loyal to the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"我必须忠于任务。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/47
msgid ""
"...Next.\n"
msgstr ""
"……下一个。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/48
msgid ""
"There is a snake in the bushes. It is poisonous. I\n"
"need you to get rid of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"灌木丛里有一条蛇。它有毒。我\n"
"需要你去把它除掉。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/49
msgid ""
"I chase it back to its nest.\n"
msgstr ""
"我追它回巢。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/50
msgid ""
"You can't. The snake's too vicious. It's already\n"
"killed many people.\n"
msgstr ""
"你做不到。那条蛇太凶残了。它已经\n"
"杀了好多人。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/51
msgid ""
"...I chase it away.\n"
msgstr ""
"……我把它赶走。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/52
msgid ""
"It will bite you unless you kill it.\n"
msgstr ""
"你不杀它，它就会咬你。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/53
msgid ""
"Go home!\n"
msgstr ""
"回家去！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/54
msgid ""
"...Kill me... Kill me now...\n"
msgstr ""
"……杀了我……现在就杀了我……\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/55
msgid ""
"Why not kill the snake? Your mission is to get rid\n"
"of it.\n"
msgstr ""
"为何不杀蛇？任务就是\n"
"除掉它。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/56
msgid ""
"Is this what you call loyalty?\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是你说的忠诚？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/57
msgid ""
"What are you loyal to? Country? Ideology?\n"
"Feelings?\n"
msgstr ""
"你忠于啥？国家？思想？\n"
"感情？\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/58
msgid ""
"I... I...\n"
msgstr ""
"我……我……\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/59
msgid ""
"I am loyal to myself.\n"
msgstr ""
"我忠于自己。\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/60
msgid ""
"...Who's there?!\n"
msgstr ""
"……谁？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/61
msgid ""
"Who's that?!\n"
msgstr ""
"谁？！\n"

#: codec/1/257/0x101110/62
msgid ""
"Intruder!\n"
msgstr ""
"有入侵者！\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/0
msgid ""
"I'm about to leave for Costa Rica, a place\n"
"completely unfamiliar to me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我即将前往哥斯达黎加，\n"
"一个完全陌生的地方。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/1
msgid ""
"And on a top-secret mission for the CIA, no less.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且还是为中情局执行绝密任务。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/2
msgid ""
"No guarantees I'll come back alive. Might even get\n"
"rubbed out by the CIA itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"能不能活着回来没有保证，\n"
"甚至可能被中情局灭口。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/3
msgid ""
"So I'm leaving behind this record, for her sake... for\n"
"The Boss' honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以我留下这份记录，为她……\n"
"也为The Boss的荣光。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/4
msgid ""
"Ever since I was a child, I've loved to look up at\n"
"the night sky.\n"
msgstr ""
"从小我就喜欢\n"
"仰望夜空。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/5
msgid ""
"I'd go outside after sunset and drink in the cold air.\n"
msgstr ""
"日落后出门，呼吸寒冷的空气。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/6
msgid ""
"The moon, Venus, so many stars floating on the\n"
"edge of infinity...\n"
msgstr ""
"月亮、金星，无数星辰\n"
"漂浮在无垠的边际……\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/7
msgid ""
"In Manchester, it wasn't very often you saw the\n"
"night sky in all its star-studded glory.\n"
msgstr ""
"在曼彻斯特，很少能见到\n"
"满天繁星的夜空。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/8
msgid ""
"But it was enough to stir a deep longing inside me.\n"
msgstr ""
"但那已足以唤起我深深的向往。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/9
msgid ""
"Even as others cowered beneath Nazi air raids,\n"
msgstr ""
"即使在别人躲着纳粹空袭时，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/10
msgid ""
"I was out there watching the skies, dreaming of\n"
"one day reaching the heavens.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也在外面仰望天空，\n"
"梦想有朝一日飞向太空。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/11
msgid ""
"There were, of course, more practical concerns.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，还有更现实的原因。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/12
msgid ""
"My skin was incredibly sensitive. Even the slightest\n"
"bit of sun would turn it an angry shade of red.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的皮肤异常敏感，\n"
"稍微晒点太阳就会红肿发炎。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/13
msgid ""
"Playing outside during the day was completely out\n"
"of the question.\n"
msgstr ""
"白天在外面玩\n"
"根本不可能。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/14
msgid ""
"Naturally, I hardly ever had the chance to play with\n"
"other children my age.\n"
msgstr ""
"自然，我几乎没机会\n"
"和同龄的孩子一起玩。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/15
msgid ""
"But I never felt lonely for it.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我并不觉得寂寞。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/16
msgid ""
"Their way of thinking was irrational, making them\n"
"simple, easy to predict.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们的思维毫无逻辑，\n"
"简单又容易预测。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/17
msgid ""
"The boys would talk of tanks and aeroplanes and\n"
"creepy, crawly bugs...\n"
msgstr ""
"男孩们谈论坦克、飞机\n"
"和爬来爬去的小虫……\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/18
msgid ""
"the girls of pretty dresses, glass beads and tea\n"
"and cakes. Of boys they liked...\n"
msgstr ""
"女孩们谈论漂亮的裙子、玻璃珠、\n"
"茶点，还有喜欢的男生……\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/19
msgid ""
"I never had much to say on such matters.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些话题我无话可说。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/20
msgid ""
"The curious thing is, adults really aren't all that\n"
"different.\n"
msgstr ""
"奇怪的是，大人其实\n"
"也没什么两样。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/21
msgid ""
"They're simple, capricious. Especially men.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们简单又善变。男人尤其如此。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/22
msgid ""
"As they get older, their heads fill with thoughts of\n"
"women and more women.\n"
msgstr ""
"年纪越大，他们脑子里\n"
"就越是塞满了女人。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/23
msgid ""
"Thankfully, I always did have a head for\n"
"mathematics.\n"
msgstr ""
"好在我在数学上\n"
"一直很有天分。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/24
msgid ""
"When I was about ten, I'd visit a Dr. Turing, who\n"
"lived nearby.\n"
msgstr ""
"十岁左右，我常去拜访\n"
"住在附近的图灵博士。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/25
msgid ""
"We'd sit and discuss mathematical logic.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们坐在一起讨论数理逻辑。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/26
msgid ""
"The lights were always on at his house, even in the\n"
"dead of night.\n"
msgstr ""
"他家总是亮着灯，\n"
"即使在深夜。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/27
msgid ""
"\"Theoretically,\" he'd say, \"there's no algorithm that\n"
"a computing machine couldn't reproduce.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「从理论上讲，」他常说，\n"
"「没有计算机无法复现的算法。」\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/28
msgid ""
"Dr. Turing wasn't foolish like other men,\n"
msgstr ""
"图灵博士不像别的男人那么愚蠢，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/29
msgid ""
"although I didn't find out why until later... after he\n"
"died.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽管我是很久以后，\n"
"在他死后才知道原因……\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/30
msgid ""
"\"The time will come,\" he'd say, \"when computers will\n"
"be able to think for themselves.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「总有一天，」他常说，\n"
"「计算机能自己思考。」\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/31
msgid ""
"That idea rocked me to my core.\n"
msgstr ""
"这个想法深深震撼了我。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/32
msgid ""
"My aptitude for mathematics brought me closer to\n"
"the stars.\n"
msgstr ""
"我的数学天赋\n"
"让我离星星更近。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/33
msgid ""
"I breezed through school, then went to America for\n"
"university.\n"
msgstr ""
"我一路跳级，\n"
"又去美国念了大学。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/34
msgid ""
"While I was studying at Caltech, NASA was\n"
"established.\n"
msgstr ""
"我在加州理工读书时，\n"
"NASA成立了。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/35
msgid ""
"I signed up in a heartbeat.\n"
msgstr ""
"我立刻报了名。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/36
msgid ""
"I was a pretty good computer engineer at the time,\n"
"and NASA needed skills like mine.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时我是个不错的计算机工程师，\n"
"NASA正需要我这样的技术。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/37
msgid ""
"The work was enjoyable. Even though I'd given up\n"
"on going into space myself,\n"
msgstr ""
"工作很愉快。虽然我已放弃\n"
"自己飞上太空，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/38
msgid ""
"it was a pleasure just being a part of it all.\n"
msgstr ""
"能参与其中就已足够快乐。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/39
msgid ""
"I was assigned to Project Mercury, America's effort\n"
"to compete with the Soviets in manned space flight.\n"
msgstr ""
"我被分到水星计划——美国为\n"
"与苏联竞逐载人航天而设的项目。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/40
msgid ""
"Seven men were chosen as pilot candidates for\n"
"the program,\n"
msgstr ""
"七个人被选为\n"
"该计划的飞行员候选人，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/41
msgid ""
"becoming heroes overnight. People called them the\n"
"\"Mercury Seven.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"一夜之间成了英雄。\n"
"人称「水星七杰」。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/42
msgid ""
"The project made good progress, more or less. We\n"
"had all the funds and materials we needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"项目进展大体顺利，\n"
"资金和物资都很充足。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/43
msgid ""
"After countless hours of analysis, we even had\n"
"plans for something on par with Sputnik.\n"
msgstr ""
"经过无数小时的分析，\n"
"我们甚至做出了对标斯普特尼克的方案。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/44
msgid ""
"We thought it'd be only a matter of time before we\n"
"caught up with the Russians.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们以为追上苏联人\n"
"只是时间问题。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/45
msgid ""
"They'd sent a dog into orbit and brought it back\n"
"safely to Earth.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们把一条狗送上轨道，\n"
"又安全地带回了地球。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/46
msgid ""
"But NASA top brass dismissed that success as a\n"
"fluke.\n"
msgstr ""
"可NASA的高层把这次成功\n"
"当成侥幸。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/47
msgid ""
"The Americans recovered their reentry capsules at\n"
"sea.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国人在海上\n"
"回收他们的返回舱。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/48
msgid ""
"But the only ocean bordering the Soviet Union is\n"
"the Arctic,\n"
msgstr ""
"但苏联濒临的海洋\n"
"只有北冰洋，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/49
msgid ""
"so their reentry capsules had to make impact on\n"
"land.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以他们的返回舱\n"
"只能在陆地上着陆。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/50
msgid ""
"A dog was one thing, but human spaceflight would\n"
"still take some time. Or so we thought.\n"
msgstr ""
"送狗是一回事，载人飞行\n"
"还得等些时日。当时我们这么想。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/51
msgid ""
"At the end of January 1961, we successfully put a\n"
"chimpanzee named Ham into orbit.\n"
msgstr ""
"1961年1月底，我们成功把\n"
"一只叫哈姆的黑猩猩送上轨道。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/52
msgid ""
"He returned to Earth as healthy as ever.\n"
msgstr ""
"它回到地球时健康如初。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/53
msgid ""
"NASA was giddy with success.\n"
msgstr ""
"NASA沉浸在成功的喜悦里。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/54
msgid ""
"It was then that a new woman showed up for duty.\n"
"She was a backup pilot and advisor.\n"
msgstr ""
"就在这时，一位新女性到任。\n"
"她是后备飞行员兼顾问。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/55
msgid ""
"She was beautiful, with blond hair, a strong mouth,\n"
"and a steely gaze.\n"
msgstr ""
"她很美，金发，嘴唇坚毅，\n"
"目光如钢。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/56
msgid ""
"But there was something else in those eyes,\n"
msgstr ""
"但那双眼睛里还有别的东西，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/57
msgid ""
"a twinkle of something warmer... of affection.\n"
msgstr ""
"一丝更温暖的光……是温情。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/58
msgid ""
"It was The Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是THE BOSS。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/59
msgid ""
"She took one look at us in our revelry and\n"
"murmured:\n"
msgstr ""
"她看了眼狂欢的我们，\n"
"低声说道：\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/60
msgid ""
"\"Savor this joy today. Because tomorrow you'll\n"
"have to face the truth.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“今天就尽情欢喜吧。因为明天\n"
"你们就得面对真相。”\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/61
msgid ""
"And she was right.\n"
msgstr ""
"而她说中了。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/62
msgid ""
"The next day, our project schedule was\n"
"accelerated.\n"
msgstr ""
"第二天，我们的项目进度\n"
"就被提前了。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/63
msgid ""
"We'd received new information that the Soviets\n"
"were mere months away from putting a man into\n"
"space.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们收到新情报：苏联\n"
"距离把人送上太空\n"
"只剩几个月了。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/64
msgid ""
"The brass had misjudged the Russians.\n"
msgstr ""
"高层错估了俄国人。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/65
msgid ""
"We couldn't afford to allow the shock of another\n"
"Sputnik.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们再也承受不起\n"
"另一个斯普特尼克的冲击。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/66
msgid ""
"Somehow, we had to get a man into space before\n"
"the Russians did.\n"
msgstr ""
"无论如何，我们必须抢在\n"
"俄国人之前把人送上太空。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/67
msgid ""
"It was an utterly impossible task. We'd only just put\n"
"our first chimp up.\n"
msgstr ""
"这根本是不可能的任务。我们\n"
"才刚把第一只猩猩送上去。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/68
msgid ""
"With a human on board, failure was not an option.\n"
msgstr ""
"载人飞行，绝不允许失败。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/69
msgid ""
"Especially if it were one of the \"Mercury Seven\"\n"
"golden boys.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其如果搭乘的是“水星七杰”\n"
"里的天之骄子。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/70
msgid ""
"And on top of that, the brass wanted to put a\n"
"window in the spacecraft.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且高层还要求在飞船上\n"
"开一扇窗。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/71
msgid ""
"The pilot wouldn't be a test animal this time, they\n"
"said.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们说，这次飞行员\n"
"不是试验动物。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/72
msgid ""
"And when this hero came back alive and well, they\n"
"wanted him to describe what he'd seen.\n"
msgstr ""
"等这位英雄平安归来，他们要\n"
"他亲口描述所见的一切。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/73
msgid ""
"It was madness.\n"
msgstr ""
"简直是疯了。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/74
msgid ""
"Adding a window to our existing spacecraft would\n"
"leave it unable to handle the stress.\n"
msgstr ""
"在现有飞船上加窗，机身\n"
"就承受不住应力。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/75
msgid ""
"Not to mention the problem of shielding the\n"
"occupant from cosmic rays.\n"
msgstr ""
"更别说还要为乘员\n"
"屏蔽宇宙射线。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/76
msgid ""
"But The Boss rose to the task, and splendidly.\n"
msgstr ""
"但THE BOSS接下了难题，而且干得漂亮。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/77
msgid ""
"She claimed to be a layman when it came to\n"
"space,\n"
msgstr ""
"她自称在航天方面\n"
"是外行，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/78
msgid ""
"but caught on keenly to new ideas and concepts.\n"
msgstr ""
"却对新概念领悟得极快。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/79
msgid ""
"She was demanding - of herself and of others.\n"
msgstr ""
"她很严格——对自己，对别人。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/80
msgid ""
"She seemed rather cold-hearted at times.\n"
msgstr ""
"有时她显得相当冷酷。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/81
msgid ""
"But I was smitten. She was beautiful, yes, but more\n"
"than that she was wise.\n"
msgstr ""
"可我着了迷。她很美，但更\n"
"重要的是她有智慧。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/82
msgid ""
"Her mind was thoroughly rational,\n"
msgstr ""
"她的思维完全理性，\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/83
msgid ""
"and yet no matter how I tried, I could never predict\n"
"her actions.\n"
msgstr ""
"可无论我怎么想，都猜不透\n"
"她的下一步。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/84
msgid ""
"It was easy for me to assume that her judgments\n"
"were drawn from an enormous base of knowledge.\n"
msgstr ""
"我很容易认为，她的判断来\n"
"自庞大的知识积累。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/85
msgid ""
"Quite simply, her life experiences were more\n"
"diverse - more intense - than anyone else's.\n"
msgstr ""
"说白了，她的人生经历比任何\n"
"人都更复杂、更激烈。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/86
msgid ""
"To me, they seemed boundless in their breadth.\n"
msgstr ""
"在我看来，那广博没有边际。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/87
msgid ""
"In her, I saw a reflection of the night sky.\n"
msgstr ""
"我在她身上看见了夜空的倒影。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/88
msgid ""
"Perhaps because I too was a woman, she and I\n"
"became close.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许因为同为女性，我和她\n"
"亲近了起来。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/89
msgid ""
"I couldn't go out in the sun, but she lit up my life.\n"
msgstr ""
"我见不得阳光，她却照亮了我的生活。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/90
msgid ""
"Her light was soft, like that of the moon. I was so\n"
"happy.\n"
msgstr ""
"她的光很柔和，像月光。\n"
"我那时多幸福啊。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/91
msgid ""
"With her unerring guidance, the project steadily\n"
"regained its footing.\n"
msgstr ""
"在她精准的指引下，项目\n"
"逐渐重回正轨。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/92
msgid ""
"But one issue remained - the pilot's safety.\n"
msgstr ""
"但还有一个问题——飞行员的安全。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/93
msgid ""
"When the day came to choose a pilot, the Mercury\n"
"Seven just quietly walked out.\n"
msgstr ""
"到了选飞行员那天，水星七杰\n"
"只是默默走了出去。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/94
msgid ""
"Who could blame them? It was far too great a risk\n"
"to take.\n"
msgstr ""
"谁能怪他们？那风险\n"
"实在太大了。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/95
msgid ""
"Even if they'd volunteered, NASA would never have\n"
"let them go.\n"
msgstr ""
"就算他们自愿，NASA也绝\n"
"不会放人。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/96
msgid ""
"They were national heroes, basking in the media\n"
"spotlight.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们是国家英雄，正沐浴在\n"
"媒体的聚光灯下。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/97
msgid ""
"There was no way they'd be sent on such a\n"
"mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"绝不可能派他们去执行\n"
"这种任务。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/98
msgid ""
"The conference room was silent.\n"
msgstr ""
"会议室一片寂静。\n"

#: codec/1/258/0x102280/99
msgid ""
"Then, slowly, she raised her hand - almost as if\n"
"acting out a scene from a movie.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后，她缓缓举起手——\n"
"像在演电影里的一个镜头。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/0
msgid ""
"I spoke out against her going,\n"
msgstr ""
"我曾反对让她去，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/1
msgid ""
"submitting a report stating the ray shielding was\n"
"inadequate.\n"
msgstr ""
"并提交报告指出\n"
"射线防护不足。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/2
msgid ""
"But the brass's response was brusque:\n"
msgstr ""
"但上层的回复很生硬：\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/3
msgid ""
"\"She's already been exposed to a nuclear test in\n"
"Nevada. She's the perfect candidate.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「她在内华达已经经历过核试验。\n"
"她是最佳人选。」\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/4
msgid ""
"It was completely irrational.\n"
msgstr ""
"这完全不讲道理。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/5
msgid ""
"Repeated exposure to radiation would only\n"
"increase the danger.\n"
msgstr ""
"反复接受辐射\n"
"只会增加危险。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/6
msgid ""
"But the government was still reeling from the\n"
"Soviets' success with Sputnik.\n"
msgstr ""
"可政府仍被苏联的\n"
"斯普特尼克成功打击着。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/7
msgid ""
"There was no hope of getting a rational response.\n"
"They were simply too panicked.\n"
msgstr ""
"别指望得到理性的回应。\n"
"他们只是太慌乱了。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/8
msgid ""
"People can be so obtuse when it comes to things\n"
"they can't see.\n"
msgstr ""
"对于看不见的东西，\n"
"人们总是如此迟钝。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/9
msgid ""
"I, however, understood all too well.\n"
msgstr ""
"而我再清楚不过。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/10
msgid ""
"Just as invisible ultraviolet radiation scorched my\n"
"skin,\n"
msgstr ""
"正如看不见的紫外线\n"
"会灼伤我的皮肤，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/11
msgid ""
"heavy particle radiation from space would cause\n"
"irreparable harm to human tissue.\n"
msgstr ""
"来自太空的重粒子辐射\n"
"会给人体组织造成不可逆的伤害。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/12
msgid ""
"In a word, she was expendable.\n"
msgstr ""
"一句话，她是可以牺牲的。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/13
msgid ""
"It was during The Boss's pre-flight checkup\n"
msgstr ""
"在The Boss的飞行前体检中，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/14
msgid ""
"that I noticed something strange on the X-ray of\n"
"her skull.\n"
msgstr ""
"我发现她头骨X光片上\n"
"有些异常。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/15
msgid ""
"Part of the right hemisphere of her brain was\n"
"damaged.\n"
msgstr ""
"她右脑的一部分\n"
"受到了损伤。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/16
msgid ""
"It seemed inexplicable given her keen intelligence\n"
"and amazing physical prowess.\n"
msgstr ""
"以她敏锐的头脑和惊人的体能，\n"
"这实在匪夷所思。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/17
msgid ""
"But there it was, and I decided to report it.\n"
msgstr ""
"可事实就在眼前，我决定上报。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/18
msgid ""
"I hoped that perhaps my discovery of a physical\n"
"defect\n"
msgstr ""
"我希望，发现这种\n"
"身体缺陷\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/19
msgid ""
"would result in the flight being canceled.\n"
msgstr ""
"能让这次飞行被取消。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/20
msgid ""
"...But as I went to make my report, she stopped me.\n"
msgstr ""
"……可我正要去报告时，她拦住了我。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/21
msgid ""
"\"Why?\" I demanded. \"How can you let yourself be\n"
"their guinea pig?!\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「为什么？」我质问道。\n"
"「你怎么能当他们的试验品？！」\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/22
msgid ""
"Ignoring my protests, she took me up to the roof\n"
"of the lab.\n"
msgstr ""
"她不顾我的反对，\n"
"把我带到了实验室天台。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/23
msgid ""
"The night sky was ablaze with stars.\n"
msgstr ""
"夜空中繁星闪烁。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/24
msgid ""
"It was there that I learned how she had wounded\n"
"her head.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是在那里，我得知了\n"
"她头部受伤的缘由。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/25
msgid ""
"1943, Los Alamos.\n"
msgstr ""
"1943年，洛斯阿拉莫斯。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/26
msgid ""
"She was serving with the Special Forces when she\n"
"received new orders.\n"
msgstr ""
"她在特种部队服役时\n"
"接到了新命令。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/27
msgid ""
"A German spy had infiltrated the Manhattan Project,\n"
msgstr ""
"一名德国间谍渗入了曼哈顿计划，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/28
msgid ""
"which aimed to build the world's first atomic bomb.\n"
"She was to eliminate him.\n"
msgstr ""
"那项计划要造出世界第一颗\n"
"原子弹。她要去除掉他。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/29
msgid ""
"His name was John von Neumann, a mathematician\n"
"with superhuman computational abilities,\n"
msgstr ""
"他叫约翰·冯·诺依曼，一位\n"
"计算能力超人的数学家，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/30
msgid ""
"and the designer of the explosive lens.\n"
msgstr ""
"也是爆缩透镜的设计者。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/31
msgid ""
"The Manhattan Project was a top national priority,\n"
"security accordingly tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"曼哈顿计划是国家最高机密，\n"
"安保自然严密。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/32
msgid ""
"The guards couldn't be allowed to know what was\n"
"going on.\n"
msgstr ""
"不能让守卫知道\n"
"到底发生了什么。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/33
msgid ""
"She'd have to slip past them and make the death\n"
"look like an accident.\n"
msgstr ""
"她得绕过他们，让那场死亡\n"
"看起来像意外。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/34
msgid ""
"...It should have been an easy enough mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"……本该是个轻松的任务。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/35
msgid ""
"But just before the operation, she received\n"
"unexpected news:\n"
msgstr ""
"但就在行动前，她收到\n"
"一个意外的消息：\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/36
msgid ""
"a new life was growing inside her.\n"
msgstr ""
"她体内正孕育着新的生命。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/37
msgid ""
"She was overcome with joy. And for one brief\n"
"moment, it clouded her judgment.\n"
msgstr ""
"她欣喜若狂。而那一瞬间，\n"
"喜悦蒙蔽了她的判断。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/38
msgid ""
"She accidentally got into a shootout with the\n"
"guards, and without thinking protected her belly.\n"
msgstr ""
"她意外与守卫交火，下意识\n"
"护住了自己的肚子。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/39
msgid ""
"She was shot in the head.\n"
msgstr ""
"她头部中弹。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/40
msgid ""
"The bullet only grazed the surface of her brain,\n"
msgstr ""
"子弹只擦过大脑表层，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/41
msgid ""
"but the tissue around the wound was destroyed,\n"
"leaving her in a coma.\n"
msgstr ""
"但伤口周围的组织被毁，\n"
"她陷入了昏迷。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/42
msgid ""
"She wasn't given much chance of recovery. But\n"
"three months later, she woke up.\n"
msgstr ""
"没人看好她能康复。\n"
"可三个月后，她醒了过来。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/43
msgid ""
"Within six, she was able to move around as if\n"
"nothing had happened.\n"
msgstr ""
"六个月后，她已行动自如，\n"
"仿佛什么都没发生过。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/44
msgid ""
"It was functional compensation\n"
msgstr ""
"这是功能代偿\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/45
msgid ""
"- the other parts of her brain took over for the\n"
"part that was lost.\n"
msgstr ""
"——大脑其他部位顶替了\n"
"受损的部分。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/46
msgid ""
"It made logical sense. But such a full recovery was\n"
"nothing short of a miracle.\n"
msgstr ""
"这合乎逻辑。但恢复得如此\n"
"彻底，堪称奇迹。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/47
msgid ""
"Perhaps her superhuman willpower made it\n"
"possible. Or perhaps...\n"
msgstr ""
"也许是她超人的意志力\n"
"做到了。又或许……\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/48
msgid ""
"\"Perhaps my body knew it had to survive for the\n"
"sake of my unborn child.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“也许我的身体知道，\n"
"为了腹中的孩子必须活下去。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/49
msgid ""
"She smiled as she said that... I understand how\n"
"she must have felt.\n"
msgstr ""
"她说这话时笑了……我懂她\n"
"当时的心情。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/50
msgid ""
"\"Some have taken to calling me 'Ms. Left Lobe,\"\n"
"she said.\n"
msgstr ""
"“有人开始叫我‘左脑女士’，”\n"
"她说道。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/51
msgid ""
"\"Because I'll do anything for the mission.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“因为为了任务，我什么都做。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/52
msgid ""
"She was tough, yes. But she had feelings, too. I\n"
"knew that better than anyone else.\n"
msgstr ""
"她确实坚强。但她也有感情。\n"
"这点我比谁都清楚。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/53
msgid ""
"As it turned out, von Neumann wasn't the spy.\n"
msgstr ""
"结果证明，冯·诺依曼不是间谍。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/54
msgid ""
"The assassination order was a deliberate bit of\n"
"misinformation planted by the Russians.\n"
msgstr ""
"那份暗杀命令，是俄国人\n"
"故意放出的假情报。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/55
msgid ""
"She had been deceived.\n"
msgstr ""
"她被骗了。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/56
msgid ""
"The Eastern and Western camps were united on\n"
"one point - opposition to the Nazis.\n"
msgstr ""
"东西方阵营在一点上一致：\n"
"反对纳粹。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/57
msgid ""
"The Allies needed to develop that bomb before\n"
"Hitler did.\n"
msgstr ""
"盟军必须抢在希特勒之前\n"
"造出那颗炸弹。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/58
msgid ""
"But in looking ahead,\n"
msgstr ""
"但放眼未来，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/59
msgid ""
"the Russians found the Manhattan Project's\n"
"progress a little too quick for their liking.\n"
msgstr ""
"俄国人觉得曼哈顿计划的\n"
"进展快得让他们不舒服。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/60
msgid ""
"Mass-production of a uranium bomb like the one\n"
"that was eventually dropped on Hiroshima\n"
msgstr ""
"像后来投在广岛那样的铀弹，\n"
"要量产并不容易。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/61
msgid ""
"would be difficult from a material perspective.\n"
msgstr ""
"从材料角度看很困难。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/62
msgid ""
"But a plutonium bomb, once perfected, could be\n"
"mass-produced and eventually even miniaturized.\n"
msgstr ""
"但钚弹一旦成熟，就能量产，\n"
"甚至最终小型化。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/63
msgid ""
"...And Moscow did not like the idea of America\n"
"having that kind of head start.\n"
msgstr ""
"……而莫斯科不喜欢美国\n"
"领先这么多。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/64
msgid ""
"Explosive lens technology was critical to the\n"
"plutonium design.\n"
msgstr ""
"爆缩透镜技术是钚弹设计的\n"
"关键。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/65
msgid ""
"So the plan was to get rid of its pioneer, von\n"
"Neumann.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以计划除掉它的开创者\n"
"冯·诺依曼。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/66
msgid ""
"And when that plot came to light, the U.S. and the\n"
"Soviet Union parted ways for good.\n"
msgstr ""
"阴谋败露后，美苏就此\n"
"彻底分道扬镳。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/67
msgid ""
"It was one of the rare cold nights in Florida.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是佛罗里达少有的寒夜。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/68
msgid ""
"She put her arm gently around my shivering\n"
"shoulders.\n"
msgstr ""
"她轻轻搂住我\n"
"颤抖的肩膀。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/69
msgid ""
"As I listened to her voice, I was wrapped in her\n"
"soothing scent.\n"
msgstr ""
"听着她的声音，我被她\n"
"安心的气息包围。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/70
msgid ""
"I felt as if I were dreaming.\n"
msgstr ""
"我恍若身处梦中。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/71
msgid ""
"Even in failure, she seemed perfect\n"
msgstr ""
"即便失败，她也完美无缺\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/72
msgid ""
"- oddly enough, the failed assassination attempt\n"
"helped preserve America's edge...\n"
msgstr ""
"——说来讽刺，那次失败的暗杀\n"
"反倒保住了美国的优势……\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/73
msgid ""
"A true super genius,\n"
msgstr ""
"一位真正的超级天才，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/74
msgid ""
"von Neumann went on to make his mark in\n"
"numerous fields outside of the Manhattan Project.\n"
msgstr ""
"冯·诺依曼后来在曼哈顿计划\n"
"之外的众多领域都留下名字。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/75
msgid ""
"Economic game theory, stored-program computing...\n"
msgstr ""
"经济博弈论、存储程序计算……\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/76
msgid ""
"Almost all computers today use stored programs,\n"
msgstr ""
"今天几乎所有电脑都用存储程序，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/77
msgid ""
"the so-called \"Von Neumann architecture.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"也就是所谓的“冯·诺依曼架构”。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/78
msgid ""
"His death would have set back computing 10 years,\n"
msgstr ""
"他若死了，计算技术会倒退十年，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/79
msgid ""
"and I wouldn't be at NASA doing research.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不会在NASA做研究。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/80
msgid ""
"I wouldn't have been there - in her arms - that\n"
"night.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不会在那个夜晚——\n"
"躺在她的怀里。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/81
msgid ""
"I thanked the fates for giving me that chance.\n"
msgstr ""
"我感谢命运给了我那个机会。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/82
msgid ""
"But then she said something unexpected.\n"
msgstr ""
"可接着她说出一句意外的话。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/83
msgid ""
"\"I should have killed von Neumann when I had the\n"
"chance.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“我该在有机会时杀了\n"
"冯·诺依曼。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/84
msgid ""
"\"Why?\" I asked. \"Wasn't the order a Soviet plot?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“为什么？”我问，“那道命令不是苏联的阴谋吗？”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/85
msgid ""
"I looked up at her as she began to explain.\n"
msgstr ""
"我抬头看她，她开始解释。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/86
msgid ""
"\"Yes, von Neumann was innocent. And killing the\n"
"innocent is a grave crime.\n"
msgstr ""
"“是的，冯·诺依曼是无辜的。\n"
"而杀害无辜是重罪。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/87
msgid ""
"But I can't help but wonder, had I succeeded, what\n"
"would the world be like now?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"可我忍不住想，如果我成功了，\n"
"世界会变成什么样？”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/88
msgid ""
"Even without von Neumann, the explosive lens\n"
"would have eventually been developed\n"
msgstr ""
"就算没有冯·诺依曼，爆缩透镜\n"
"迟早也会造出来，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/89
msgid ""
"- Von Neumann architecture, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"——冯·诺依曼架构也一样。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/90
msgid ""
"But she seemed to believe that if progress had\n"
"been put off for a few years,\n"
msgstr ""
"可她似乎相信，如果这一切\n"
"推迟几年，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/91
msgid ""
"then perhaps East and West would have had a\n"
"chance to work hand in hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"东西方也许就有机会\n"
"携手合作。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/92
msgid ""
"I'd never considered such a possibility. But her\n"
"tone was confident, assertive.\n"
msgstr ""
"我从没想过这种可能。但她的\n"
"语气自信而笃定。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/93
msgid ""
"It was as if she intended to make the two\n"
"superpowers shake hands herself.\n"
msgstr ""
"仿佛她要亲手让两个\n"
"超级大国握手。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/94
msgid ""
"\"The explosive lens was developed too early,\n"
msgstr ""
"“爆缩透镜问世得太早，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/95
msgid ""
"spawning a Cold War and an endless nuclear arms\n"
"race,\" she continued.\n"
msgstr ""
"催生了冷战和无尽的核军备\n"
"竞赛，”她继续说道。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/96
msgid ""
"\"That mission sprung from deceit, but maybe it was\n"
"divine providence, too.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“那次任务源于欺骗，但也许\n"
"也是天意。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/97
msgid ""
"It was like she was speaking to her own child.\n"
msgstr ""
"她像是在对自己的孩子说话。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/98
msgid ""
"Her large, warm hand was on my head.\n"
msgstr ""
"她那只大而温暖的手放在我头上。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/99
msgid ""
"\"I failed the mission because I let the mother in me\n"
"take over.\n"
msgstr ""
"“我任务失败，是因为让\n"
"母亲的本能占了上风。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/100
msgid ""
"I should have killed him, no matter how great the\n"
"guilt.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我该杀了他，无论背负多大的\n"
"罪疚。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/101
msgid ""
"\"If I'd killed him, I might not have prevented\n"
"Hiroshima,\n"
msgstr ""
"“如果我杀了他，也许阻止不了\n"
"广岛，\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/102
msgid ""
"but maybe I could have saved everyone in\n"
"Nagasaki...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"但也许能救下长崎的\n"
"所有人……”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/103
msgid ""
"I looked up at her and saw her looking up, too... up\n"
"at the starry sky.\n"
msgstr ""
"我抬头看她，发现她也在仰望……\n"
"仰望星空。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/104
msgid ""
"Her face showed only deep remorse.\n"
msgstr ""
"她脸上只有深深的悔恨。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/105
msgid ""
"It was as if she'd convinced herself that she alone\n"
"was responsible for creating this twisted world...\n"
msgstr ""
"仿佛她认定，这个扭曲的世界\n"
"全是由她一人造成的……\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/106
msgid ""
"\"But that's no reason for you to sacrifice yourself\n"
"for this.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“但这不是你为此牺牲自己的\n"
"理由。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/107
msgid ""
"I knew I'd never dissuade her. And yet I still clung\n"
"to hope.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道劝不动她。可我仍\n"
"抱着希望。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/108
msgid ""
"\"I know you're concerned, and I thank you. But I\n"
"have to be loyal to the end.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“我知道你在担心，谢谢你。\n"
"但我必须忠诚到底。”\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/109
msgid ""
"And then she smiled at me.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后她对我笑了。\n"

#: codec/1/260/0x104860/110
msgid ""
"Loyal to the end... \"Loyal to what?\" I asked. But she\n"
"didn't answer.\n"
msgstr ""
"忠诚到底……“对什么忠诚？”\n"
"我问。她没有回答。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/0
msgid ""
"The days that followed were spent training\n"
"tirelessly for our first space flight.\n"
msgstr ""
"接下来的日子都用来\n"
"为首次太空飞行不懈训练。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/1
msgid ""
"The Boss endured conditioning that tested the\n"
"limits of human capability,\n"
msgstr ""
"The Boss承受着挑战\n"
"人体极限的训练，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/2
msgid ""
"and I supported her. Those were happy days.\n"
msgstr ""
"我负责支持她。那段日子很幸福。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/3
msgid ""
"On April 12th, the spacecraft carrying The Boss\n"
"left the Earth's atmosphere.\n"
msgstr ""
"4月12日，搭载The Boss的飞船\n"
"飞出了地球大气层。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/4
msgid ""
"Although it was only 20 minutes of ballistic flight,\n"
"it was nothing short of miraculous,\n"
msgstr ""
"虽然只是20分钟的弹道飞行，\n"
"却堪称奇迹，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/5
msgid ""
"considering how little time we'd had. The first\n"
"human in space. We were ecstatic.\n"
msgstr ""
"毕竟我们准备时间太短。\n"
"第一个进入太空的人类。我们欣喜若狂。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/6
msgid ""
"Then something went wrong.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后出了问题。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/7
msgid ""
"The reentry angle was slightly off, warping the\n"
"outer hull.\n"
msgstr ""
"再入角度略有偏差，\n"
"外壳发生了变形。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/8
msgid ""
"The cause was clear - it was the\n"
"hastily-constructed window we'd installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"原因很清楚——\n"
"就是那个匆忙装上的舷窗。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/9
msgid ""
"Her capsule missed the projected splashdown point\n"
"by a long shot.\n"
msgstr ""
"她的返回舱\n"
"远远偏离了预定落点。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/10
msgid ""
"As we raced towards the capsule, a breaking news\n"
"broadcast came over the radio.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们赶往返回舱时，\n"
"收音机里传来一条突发新闻。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/11
msgid ""
"It was the news report of the successful launch of\n"
"the Vostock rocket,\n"
msgstr ""
"那是东方号火箭\n"
"成功发射的报道，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/12
msgid ""
"piloted by the cosmonaut Yuri Gagarin. They'd\n"
"beaten us into space by the slimmest of margins.\n"
msgstr ""
"由宇航员尤里·加加林驾驶。\n"
"他们以微弱优势抢先进入了太空。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/13
msgid ""
"When we arrived, the capsule had already\n"
"disappeared beneath the waves.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们赶到时，返回舱\n"
"已经沉入海浪之下。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/14
msgid ""
"The Boss was floating on the surface.\n"
msgstr ""
"The Boss漂浮在海面上。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/15
msgid ""
"I... can't really recall what happened next.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……记不清后来发生了什么。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/16
msgid ""
"They told me later that I gave a strange scream\n"
"and plunged into the sea,\n"
msgstr ""
"后来他们告诉我，我发出一声怪叫\n"
"就冲进了海里，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/17
msgid ""
"not caring whether my skin would burn.\n"
msgstr ""
"根本顾不上皮肤会不会灼伤。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/18
msgid ""
"She didn't wake up.\n"
msgstr ""
"她没有醒来。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/19
msgid ""
"Her entire body was bruised, burnt, scorched by\n"
"cosmic rays.\n"
msgstr ""
"她全身瘀伤、烧伤，\n"
"被宇宙射线灼烤过。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/20
#: codec/1/284/0x11c2d0/5
msgid ""
"It was a miracle she was still alive.\n"
msgstr ""
"她能活下来已是奇迹。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/21
msgid ""
"Every day, propaganda boasting of the shining\n"
"accomplishment flowed out of the Soviet Union.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联每天都在宣传\n"
"这项辉煌成就。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/22
msgid ""
"The hardest part was having to read the report\n"
"the next morning from Izvestia,\n"
msgstr ""
"最难受的是第二天早上\n"
"读到《消息报》的报道，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/23
msgid ""
"the Soviet governmental paper.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联的政府机关报。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/24
msgid ""
"Written there after the report were those\n"
"legendary words of Major Gargarin -\n"
msgstr ""
"报道之后还写着\n"
"加加林少校那句名言——\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/25
msgid ""
"\"The Earth is blue.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「地球是蓝色的。」\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/26
msgid ""
"The person who should have said those words,\n"
"though, was incapacitated, confined to a bed.\n"
msgstr ""
"可本该说出这句话的人，\n"
"却卧床不起，动弹不得。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/27
msgid ""
"NASA opted to pretend the flight had never\n"
"happened.\n"
msgstr ""
"NASA决定\n"
"当这次飞行从未发生。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/28
msgid ""
"The Soviets had orbited a man around the Earth\n"
"and returned him safely.\n"
msgstr ""
"苏联人把人送上地球轨道\n"
"又安全接了回来。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/29
msgid ""
"We'd barely managed to escape the atmosphere\n"
"and achieve ballistic flight.\n"
msgstr ""
"而我们只是勉强冲出大气层，\n"
"完成了弹道飞行。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/30
msgid ""
"Even worse, the pilot was horribly mangled and\n"
"the spacecraft lost altogether...\n"
msgstr ""
"更糟的是，飞行员重伤，\n"
"飞船也彻底丢失……\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/31
msgid ""
"As they saw it,\n"
msgstr ""
"在他们看来，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/32
msgid ""
"covering it up was the only alternative to seeing\n"
"the nation's pride dealt yet another blow.\n"
msgstr ""
"要想不让国家颜面\n"
"再受一次打击，只能掩盖。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/33
msgid ""
"I've been told\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/34
msgid ""
"military records show The Boss was taking part in\n"
"the Bay of Pigs incident at the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"军方记录显示，The Boss当时\n"
"正在参与猪湾事件。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/35
msgid ""
"They were that desperate to erase the whole affair.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们急于把整件事抹得一干二净。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/36
msgid ""
"In the end,\n"
msgstr ""
"结果，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/37
msgid ""
"Alan Shepard's ballistic flight one month later\n"
"became known as America's first space flight.\n"
msgstr ""
"一个月后艾伦·谢泼德的弹道飞行\n"
"被称为美国首次太空飞行。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/38
msgid ""
"Shepard's flight owed its success to insights\n"
"earned through The Boss's sacrifice.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢泼德的成功，\n"
"得益于The Boss牺牲换来的经验。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/39
msgid ""
"But to me, none of that mattered. I prayed day and\n"
"night for her recovery,\n"
msgstr ""
"但对我来说这些都不重要。\n"
"我日夜祈祷她康复，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/40
msgid ""
"never leaving her side, not even for a moment.\n"
msgstr ""
"片刻也不离开她身边。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/41
msgid ""
"Then, as summer ended and the chill of winter\n"
"approached, she spoke.\n"
msgstr ""
"夏去冬来，寒意渐近时，\n"
"她开口了。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/42
msgid ""
"\"Give me water...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"「给我水……」\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/43
msgid ""
"I threw myself on her breast, and she embraced me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我扑进她怀里，她也抱住了我。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/44
msgid ""
"It was all I needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就足够了。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/45
msgid ""
"I thought she would tell me about space.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为她会讲太空的事。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/46
msgid ""
"The true sky, where the stars don't twinkle.\n"
msgstr ""
"真正的天空，星星不会闪烁的天空。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/47
msgid ""
"But the only thing she'd speak of was Earth.\n"
msgstr ""
"可她只谈地球。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/48
msgid ""
"Our home - as she'd seen it from space. So\n"
"fleeting, so irreplaceable.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们的家园——她从太空看到的模样。\n"
"如此短暂，如此无可替代。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/49
msgid ""
"I was ashamed. I'd been enamored for so long with\n"
"the sky that\n"
msgstr ""
"我很羞愧。我迷恋天空太久，\n"
"以至于\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/50
msgid ""
"I'd never thought to look beneath my feet... at the\n"
"ground upon which I stood.\n"
msgstr ""
"从未想过低头看看……\n"
"脚下这片土地。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/51
msgid ""
"As soon as her rehab was over, she was gone.\n"
msgstr ""
"康复训练一结束，她就走了。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/52
msgid ""
"It happened without warning. No one informed me,\n"
"and the higher-ups wouldn't say a word.\n"
msgstr ""
"毫无预兆。没人通知我，\n"
"上层也只字不提。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/53
msgid ""
"It wasn't so strange or surprising, really.\n"
msgstr ""
"其实也不算奇怪。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/54
msgid ""
"I simply assumed she was off to complete her next\n"
"mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"我只当她是去执行\n"
"下一个任务了。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/55
msgid ""
"Because she was loyal, to the end.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为她忠诚，直到最后。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/56
msgid ""
"Since then, I've devoted myself to researching\n"
"artificial intelligence,\n"
msgstr ""
"从那以后，我一心投入\n"
"人工智能的研究，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/57
msgid ""
"so that no one will ever have to make her sacrifice\n"
"again.\n"
msgstr ""
"只为不再有人被迫做出\n"
"她那样的牺牲。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/58
msgid ""
"No human being should be asked to take on a\n"
"mission that dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"不该让任何人去承担那样\n"
"危险的任务。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/59
msgid ""
"Next time, I'll be the light that shines on someone\n"
"else...\n"
msgstr ""
"下一次，我要成为\n"
"照亮别人的光……\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/60
msgid ""
"I still wonder why she opened up to me on that\n"
"chilly night in Florida.\n"
msgstr ""
"我至今不明白，她为何在\n"
"佛罗里达那个寒夜向我倾诉。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/61
msgid ""
"That operation was top secret, even if it was all in\n"
"the past.\n"
msgstr ""
"那次行动是最高机密，哪怕\n"
"早已是往事。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/62
msgid ""
"I like to think it was because she trusted me... but\n"
"that's probably not the case.\n"
msgstr ""
"我宁愿相信是因为她信任我……\n"
"但恐怕并非如此。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/63
msgid ""
"She wanted someone to listen. And I don't think\n"
"that someone was me.\n"
msgstr ""
"她想找个人倾听。而那个人\n"
"恐怕不是我。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/64
msgid ""
"Those faraway eyes, the tone of her voice - like\n"
"she was talking to her own child\n"
msgstr ""
"那望向远方的眼神，那语气——\n"
"像在对自己的孩子说话，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/65
msgid ""
"- those things made it clear that she was speaking\n"
"to someone else.\n"
msgstr ""
"——这些都说明，她是在\n"
"对另一个人诉说。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/66
msgid ""
"I found myself envying that \"someone.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我竟嫉妒起那个“人”来。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/67
msgid ""
"Four years later I learned of her death. A traitor's\n"
"death, no less.\n"
msgstr ""
"四年后，我得知了她的死讯。\n"
"而且是叛徒的死法。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/68
msgid ""
"She'd stolen an American nuke and defected to\n"
"the Soviet Union,\n"
msgstr ""
"她偷走美国的核弹，\n"
"叛逃到苏联，\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/69
msgid ""
"where she was killed by her former apprentice... Or\n"
"so I was told.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后被昔日的弟子杀死……\n"
"至少他们是这么告诉我的。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/70
msgid ""
"I refused to believe it. She'd never do such a thing.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不肯相信。她绝不会做那种事。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/71
msgid ""
"I could think of only two possibilities:\n"
msgstr ""
"我只能想到两种可能：\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/72
msgid ""
"either she really was trying to bring East and West\n"
"together...\n"
msgstr ""
"一是她真的想让东西方\n"
"走到一起……\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/73
msgid ""
"Or she truly did want to be killed...\n"
msgstr ""
"二是她真的想求死……\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/74
msgid ""
"She believed the world is not the way it's\n"
"supposed to be.\n"
msgstr ""
"她认为这个世界并非它\n"
"应有的样子。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/75
msgid ""
"That it's been unbalanced by the tenuous peace\n"
"offered of nuclear deterrence.\n"
msgstr ""
"是核威慑带来的脆弱和平\n"
"让世界失衡。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/76
msgid ""
"And that she was to blame...\n"
msgstr ""
"而那都是她的错……\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/77
msgid ""
"Perhaps her death was an act of atonement.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许她的死是一种赎罪。\n"

#: codec/1/263/0x107150/78
msgid ""
"She was loyal to the end - to our world.\n"
msgstr ""
"她忠诚到底——对这个世界的忠诚。\n"
